 "notes": "No deviation: six frozen, hash-verified controllers, each once per manifest in its own fresh process on 24 fresh 128-case manifests (seeds 5025, 5041-5063), 144 cells, 18,432 episodes, no training, no selection, no extension. One naming slip before the start, with no effect on any result: the implementer first wrote the manifests under a different file name than the approved record; the ledger refused to start, the files were regenerated under the recorded names (same seeds, same cases) and nothing had run. Sustained success of 3,072: D-058 saved incumbent 1,141 (0.371), D-072 reference 1,325 (0.431), R-106 residual 1,684 (0.548), R-116 re-capture module 1,978 (0.644), R-118 continued 2,372 (0.772), R-121 JOINT 2,446 (0.796). Every one of the seven contrasts is positive after Holm with a positive paired lower bound and a drop bound within 0.05: the primary JOINT minus D-072 +0.365 [+0.344, +0.386] (lower bound above the registered +0.30; 24 of 24 manifests), JOINT minus D-058 +0.425 [+0.404, +0.446]; steps: D-072 over D-058 +0.060, R-106 over D-072 +0.117, R-116 over R-106 +0.096 (300 wins, 6 losses), R-118 over R-116 +0.128, JOINT over R-118 +0.024 [+0.008, +0.040] (17 of 24 manifests; the smallest and least uniform step). Drops of 3,072: 140 / 140 / 96 / 127 / 136 / 136: the residual removed early drops (133 -> 89) and the re-capture adds about 40-47 late drops, so JOINT's drop count equals the incumbent's. Persistent-slow failures: 1,610 / 1,446 / 1,159 / 670 / 346 / 281; what grows with the re-capture is the fast-but-unsteady class (43 for D-058, 170 for JOINT). Earlier single-study estimates are reproduced within their intervals (R-106 +0.109/+0.125 -> +0.117; R-116 +0.082/+0.094 -> +0.096; R-118 +0.104 -> +0.128; JOINT over R-118 +0.059 in R-121 -> +0.024 here, i.e. the first estimate of the joint step was high). One evaluation on one set of 24 manifests of one task and simulator; the assets are frozen but not installed: config/pen_spin/d058_fixed_stroke_incumbent is unchanged."
